# Warehouse Tabby: "Whenever an enchantment you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, create a 1/1 black Rat creature
# token with 'This token can't block.'" Bot1 Disenchants its own Flood on turn 3 and gets exactly one Rat, a 1/1 black Rat that
# cannot block: when Bot2's Grizzly Bears attacks on turn 4, blocking it with the Rat is refused while the Tabby may block.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Warehouse Tabby
Flood
Disenchant
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Grizzly Bears
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Warehouse Tabby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Flood.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Flood)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Power = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Toughness = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Colors = Black
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Token = true
[T4 Bot2.Attackers]
Bot2.Attack(Grizzly Bears > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Blockers]
! Bot1.Block(Rat Token > Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Block(Warehouse Tabby > Grizzly Bears)

[Expect]
Combat.Blocks = Warehouse Tabby > Grizzly Bears
Bot1.Graveyard = Disenchant; Flood
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Subtypes = Rat
